Contract and acceptance Record; original stage label **15a** is retained only for requirement/task/workflow IDs. [Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) is the execution authority.

Contributing packages: [Adaptive circuit policy and shared/offline acceptance](../features/Circuit-Policy.lingua); [First bounded numerical jobs and circuit references](../features/Numerical-Runtime.lingua); [Numerical equivalents and stateful model transitions](../features/Numerical-Transitions.lingua); [Powered circuit and mixed functional signals](../features/Powered-Circuit.lingua)

## Scheduling interpretation

The linked packages own implementation and its task order. This Record preserves the full source requirements, interface details, examples, research, milestones, fixtures, failure cases and completion evidence. Its `#requires` edges mean all contributors are needed to close this whole contract, not that every consumer waits for this join. Former references to earlier/later stages, delivery cycles or deferred tails describe the appropriate capability subset and composed proofs; they do not restore the removed global sequence. Incomplete unrelated siblings are not regression failures. All already verified affected capabilities must continue working.

For a mixed milestone, each contributor records its verified subset, then this join runs the actual composed workflow when all contributors exist. Do not mark the full milestone done from a local helper or silently drop geographic/hosted/numerical portions. Published exports remain usable without reopening their implementation solely to await this join; fixes to real interface defects remain mandatory.


After provider verification and implementation authorization, finish with a powered lamp and sensor circuit sharing a scene with an unconditional light and functional devices. Replace a supported circuit subsystem with a cheaper compatible model, preserve its declared external behavior, and return through a supported state transition while its authored internals remain intact.

## Required workflow milestones

- [ ] **15a.M01.** Configure and run the bounded B43/B44 circuit with explicit supply/reference, component parameters and initial conditions; inspect source-mapped voltage/current/time results. Removing the electrical supply or opening the return path changes the powered lamp; the unconditional light continues.
- [ ] **15a.M02.** Combine an idealized functional sensor with a numerical driver/load network using explicit signal/physical adapters, then replace the selected detailed subsystem with a compatible functional/equivalent model. Preserve required output timing and electrical loading within declared limits and measure the cost difference.
- [ ] **15a.M03.** Switch supported models at a synchronized boundary, preserve carried state, expose discarded/initialized state and error, and handle unsupported continuation without inventing history. Editing a detailed source invalidates its derived model; one active writer remains for each output.
- [ ] **15a.M04.** Apply a bounded automatic policy among approved alternatives, exercise validity/budget failure, and keep an offscreen causal dependency active. A pinned study never silently changes equations, and a weak visitor changes appearance without changing authoritative simulation.
- [ ] **15a.M05.** Save source/model bindings and essential run/transition evidence, reopen offline, recover interrupted execution honestly and share permitted observations without giving the visitor execution or private-source access. Preserve core responsiveness and functional behavior when a numerical activity is unavailable.

## Entry and scope

- [ ] Follow the [general delivery and acceptance rules](../Workspace-Development.lingua#dependency-driven-delivery-and-repair). Require the selected numerical package’s verified provider exports and scoped implementation authorization. Full-core acceptance and a complete material-property branch are not prerequisites for the first circuit reference. Recover 02/04/07/11a/15 handoffs; materials derivation, molecular dynamics, continuum heating and stage 20 recording are not prerequisites.
- [ ] This stage is the first consumer of the numerical run/state/authority subset documented in [stage 17 H7](Laboratory-and-adoption-contracts.lingua#h7-shared-runs-and-execution-authority), [its solver job contract](Laboratory-and-adoption-contracts.lingua#solver-job-contract), and [stage 18 K8/E5](Rigid-and-articulated-physics-contracts.lingua#k8-domains-state-observations-and-scenarios). Read those contracts as requirements, not as delivered APIs or dependencies on those stages' domain features. Implement the smallest shared services needed here; later stages extend the same services and retain their own verification obligations.
- [ ] First numerical scope: bounded DC operating points and transient resistor/capacitor/diode/switch networks with documented compact parameters, an explicit electrical reference, source/load models and a small event/threshold adapter. No transistor fabrication, field extraction, firmware/CPU emulation, arbitrary HDL execution, quantum calculation or thermal solve is implied. Extend supported models only with separate reference cases.

